e you applying as an independent applicant or on behalf of an organization?  \no Independent Applicant (if you select this choice, you will be asked to add your \nname and skip to the “Application Details” section) \no Organization  \n \n201 more lines...', extracted_content="Read from file /tmp/browser-use-downloads-eb1b0ca9/2026-Research-Grant-Program-Example-Application.pdf (7 pages, 9,338 chars).\n<content>\n--- Page 1 ---\n \nisocfoundation.org                                 \nfoundation@isocfoundation.org      \n1 \n \nResearch Grant Program \nExample Application \nNote: This is not an application form. This document is meant to provide the application \nquestions for reference purposes only. All applications must be submitted through the \nInternet Society Foundation’s grants management platform, Fluxx. If your organization is not \nalready registered, you will need to register. It may take 1-2 business days for your \nregistration to be complete so plan ahead. Applications sent by email will not be accepted. \n \n• Are you applying as an independent applicant or on behalf of an organization?  \no Independent Applicant (if you select this choice, you will be asked to add your \nname and skip to the “Application Details” section) \no Organization  \n \nOrganization Information \n \n• Organization: \n• Primary Contact: \n• Signatory Contact: \n• Additional Contact: \no Your application should have at least two different points of contact (Primary \nContact and Additional Contact). The Signatory will receive any legal \ndocuments to sign on behalf of your organization. \n• Does your organization have a bank account in the organization’s name, and can it \nreceive funds from a foundation based in the United States? (Yes/No) \no In order to receive funds from the Internet Society Foundation, an \norganization or their fiscal sponsor must have a bank account registered in \ntheir legal name. For additional guidance, please consult the grantee eligibility \ninformation on our website. \n\n--- Page 2 ---\n \nisocfoundation.org  \n@ISOC_Foundation  \n2 \n• Please demonstrate your organization's capacity to manage a grant award up to the \nrequested amount in the proposed timeframe:* \no Share examples of previous grants awarded to your organization. You can \nprovide URLs to award announcements and press releases, a copy of your \norganization’s annual budget that includes funding amounts, or other \nevidence of experience in and capacity to manage an award of this size. \n• Is the proposed project sponsored by a Fiscal Sponsor or submitted by a Fiscal Sponsor \non behalf of a Sponsored Organization?* (Select one answer) \no My organization is a Fiscal Sponsor submitting this application on behalf of a \nSponsored Organization  \no My organization is a Sponsored Organization and the proposed project will be \nsponsored by a Fiscal Sponsor \no My organization is not acting as a Fiscal Sponsor for the proposed project, nor \nsubmitting an application for a project that will be sponsored by a Fiscal Sponsor \n• Which of these statements accurately describes your organization?* \no The organization is a 501c3 nonprofit (charitable organization based in the USA). \no The organization has had Equivalency Determination (ED) status currently or in the \npast (foreign equivalent to a USA-based nonprofit) \no The organization operates exclusively for charitable purposes (i.e., as a charitable \nnongovernmental organization) but has not yet gone through the ED process. \no None of the above. \n• Please demonstrate your organization’s equivalency to a U.S. 501c3 charitable \norganization.* \no Details on how to demonstrate eligibility can be found here. In addition to \ndemonstrating that you are organized for exclusively charitable purposes, please \nensure you describe 1) whether you engage in lobbying; and, 2) how your \ngoverning documents address the usage of your organization’s assets upon \ndissolution, and whether your activities benefit private persons or non-\ncharitable organizations. If you are uploading a copy of your governing \ndocuments, please indicate the relevant sections that we should refer to. \n \n \n\n--- Page 3 ---\n \nisocfoundation.org  \n@ISOC_Foundation  \n3 \n• Please describe how most of your organization’s purpose and activities are focused on \nor related to the Internet.* \no As a supporting organization of the Internet Society (ISOC), the Internet Society \nFoundation must operate exclusively for the benefit of ISOC and follow special \nrules under U.S. tax laws.  We make grants only to organizations whose \npurpose and activities (meaning the vision, mission, articles of incorporation/by-\nlaws, core focus areas, and programming) closely relate with the \npurpose and activities of ISOC. For information on how to answer the brief \nalignment questions below, please see our website.  \n• Which of the following ISOC purposes and activities strongly aligns with your \norganization's purposes and activities?* \no Facilitate or support the technical evolution of the Internet as a research and \neducation infrastructure. \no Stimulate the community in the evolution of the Internet or educate them in its \nuse and application. \no Promote educational applications of the Internet. \no Help to promote open development, evolution or use of the Internet to benefit \npeople. \no Connect unconnected communities and individuals to the Internet.  \no Advocate for policy that is consistent with ISOC's view of the Internet.  \no Advance the development and application of Internet infrastructure, \ntechnologies, or open standards, etc. \n \n \nApplication Details \n• Project Title:* \n• Project Budget in $USD:* \n• Project Start Date:* \n• Project End Date:* \n• What is the region your project is most focused on?* \no Africa  \no Asia Pacific  \no Europe & Central Asia  \n\n--- Page 4 ---\n \nisocfoundation.org  \n@ISOC_Foundation  \n4 \no Latin America & Caribbean  \no Middle East  \no North America  \no Global \n• Which theme does your application fall under?* (Select all that apply) \no Greening the Internet \no Inclusive Internet \no Measuring Meaningful Connectivity \no Trustworthy Internet \n• Project Summary:* \n• What is the main research question you hope to test in this project?* \n• What is your research project's methodology?* \n• How do you plan on making your intended research be applicable for decision-\nmaking either by industry or government?* \n• Please describe the expected deliverables for this project.* \n• Please select the primary focus area for your project. (You can read more about our \nfocus areas by viewing the definitions of each here:) \no Affordable and Reliable Access \no Community and Partner Mobilization \no Community-Centered Connectivity \no Internet Insights and Innovation \no Online Safety and Safety \no Open and Trustworthy Internet \n \n \nObjectives and Indicators \nThese are the required indicators to measure progress towards your research project's \noutcomes. Please state the target number for each of the following outputs. \nIndicator 1: Dissemination activities share research findings with targeted audiences; \nexamples include presenting at a conference, posting on a website or social media, being \n\n--- Page 5 ---\n \nisocfoundation.org  \n@ISOC_Foundation  \n5 \npublished in a peer-reviewed journal, holding a meeting with a key stakeholder, hosting a \nworkshop or webinar to discuss the findings, etc. \n• Indicator 1: Add target number* \n \nIndicator 2: Research products include papers, webinars, blogs, videos, book chapters, etc. \n• Indicator 2: Add target number* \n \nIndicator 3: Number of collaborations with academics, industry partners and/or other \nresearchers evidenced by co-creation, resource pooling, or an interdisciplinary approach. \n• Indicator 3: Add target number* \n \nFunding Information  \n• Do you have other funds secured or requested for this project?* (Yes/No) \no If Yes - Please explain how much you are receiving/have received and for \nwhat purpose. \n• Are you currently receiving or have you in the past received any other funding from \nthe Internet Society or Internet Society Foundation? (Yes/No) \no If Yes - Please explain how much you are receiving/have received and for \nwhat purpose. \n \n \nAdditional Information:  \n• How did you hear about this grant program? (Optional):  \n \n\n--- Page 6 ---\n \nisocfoundation.org  \n@ISOC_Foundation  \n6 \nGuidance for uploading documents for your application \nApplication Documents \n \nPlease note that if the documents you are submitting are not in English, ISOC may use a \nthird-party service to translate them. Accuracy cannot be guaranteed. By submitting this \napplication, you are consenting to this practice. \nRequired: \no Completed project Budget, Workplan, and Equipment Support Form; using the \nrequired template. \n \nOrganization Documents \nRequired: \n• Tax Identification Documents: Please provide organizational tax documents, such \nas IRS Determination Letter, Form 990, or other documents that demonstrate your \nnon-profit/charitable status. \n• Governing Documents: such as Articles of Incorporation or Charter documents. If \nyou have multiple governing documents, please upload the one that most clearly \nand comprehensively outlines the organization’s purpose and activities. \n• Financial Documents: Current organizational budget, as well as the latest audits or \nnational tax returns within the last two years \nRecommended: \no Equivalency Determination: A certification that your organization is equivalent \nto a U.S. 501c3 public charity. Include only if you already have one and it is \ncurrent. \n \n\n--- Page 7 ---\n \nisocfoundation.org  \n@ISOC_Foundation  \n7 \nIf your official tax identification or governing documents are written in a non-English \nlanguage and saved in PDF, please submit the certified version in PDF as well as a Word \nversion. \nIf you encounter 