ount if available.\n</query>\n<result>\n**Funding Amount:**\nSmall grants ($5000-$50000)\n\n**Eligibility Requirements:**\nApplicants will have to demonstrate that their project addresses one or more of three criteria:\n1)  **Sustainability** – Projects that will have a lasting impact beyond the duration of the project. Examples include protecting heritage sites from desertification by creating green belts, preserving/stabilizing/restoring and adaptively reusing a historic building for community needs, researching the public heritage landscape, installing solar panels at heritage sites to generate income or decrease expenditure in the long term, building eco-friendly tourism infrastructure, direct interventions that strengthen social institutions (like traditional methods of mediation).\n2)  **Capacity development and network building** – Projects that strengthen local skills and build closer links with peer organizations in the HERITΛGE network. Examples include on-the-job training in preventive conservation (e.g., clearing or fencing sites), experience and expertise exchanges with other local NGOs on shared issues such as desertification or erosion of sites, co-operative training on museum exhibition design.\n3)  **Concrete and community impact** – Projects with strong, measurable incomes in terms of heritage protection and benefits to local people. Each project should provide clear indicators of the planned impact. Examples include increased visitation to a heritage site or program, financial benefits to the local community in terms of increased employment opportunities or local businesses created; tourism earnings; money savings by solar panel installation; the size of area protected from desertification.\n\n**How to Apply:**\nTo apply for these grants, complete the concept note application form found here: [https://heritagemanagement.jotform.com/230365681899976](https://heritagemanagement.jotform.com/230365681899976)\n\n**Full Proposal Section:**\nInformation regarding a \'Full Proposal\' section is not available in the provided content. The application process mentions completing a "concept note application form."\n</result>', extracted_content='<url>\nhttps://heritagemanagement.org/call-for-applications-small-grants-for-african-heritage-projects/\n</url>\n<query>\nExtract the \'Eligibility Requirements\' section, \'How to Apply\' section, and \'Full Proposal\' section, including any links, to gather information about eligibility, required documents, and the application process for the \'Small Grants for African Heritage Projects\'. Also, extract the funding amount if available.\n</query>\n<result>\n**Funding Amount:**\nSmall grants ($5000-$50000)\n\n**Eligibility Requirements:**\nApplicants will have to demonstrate that their project addresses one or more of three criteria:\n1)  **Sustainability** – Projects that will have a lasting impact beyond the duration of the project. Examples include protecting heritage sites from desertification by creating green belts, preserving/stabilizing/restoring and adaptively reusing a historic building for community needs, researching the public heritage landscape, installing solar panels at heritage sites to generate income or decrease expenditure in the long term, building eco-friendly tourism infrastructure, direct interventions that strengthen social institutions (like traditional methods of mediation).\n2)  **Capacity development and network building** – Projects that strengthen local skills and build closer links with peer organizations in the HERITΛGE network. Examples include on-the-job training in preventive conservation (e.g., clearing or fencing sites), experience and expertise exchanges with other local NGOs on shared issues such as desertification or erosion of sites, co-operative training on museum exhibition design.\n3)  **Concrete and community impact** – Projects with strong, measurable incomes in terms of heritage protection and benefits to local people. Each project 