ed in the provided content.\n    *   **Required Documents:** Not explicitly stated in the provided content.\n    *   **Application Process:** Use the [IMA Application Portal](https://imaresearchgrants.secure-platform.com/a/organizations/main/home) and refer to the [Guidelines for Submitting Research Proposals](https://mc-69e30ef4-758e-4371-ac6f-2657-cdn-endpoint.azureedge.net/-/media/IMA/Files/Home/Membership/Academics/IMAResearchFoundationGuidelinesOct-2025-FINAL.ashx?rev=a88a5aad59ba429990dddb8865f02ec8&hash=75506F975C0BC10972D95A01C7B8CBDB).\n\n*   **Doctoral Scholars Program**\n    *   **Description:** This program supports doctoral students at various stages in their programs.\n    *   **Award Amount:** Not explicitly stated in the provided content.\n    *   **Due Date:** Ongoing submissions are accepted.\n    *   **Eligibility:** Doctoral students.\n    *   **Required Documents:** Not explicitly stated in the provided content.\n    *   **Application Process:** Use the [IMA Application Portal](https://imaresearchgrants.secure-platform.com/a/organizations/main/home) and refer to the [Guidelines for Submitting Research Proposals](https://mc-69e30ef4-758e-4371-ac6f-2657-cdn-endpoint.azureedge.net/-/media/IMA/Files/Home/Membership/Academics/IMAResearchFoundationGuidelinesOct-2025-FINAL.ashx?rev=a88a5aad59ba429990dddb8865f02ec8&hash=75506F975C0BC10972D95A01C7B8CBDB).\n\n**Awards**\n\n*   **Distinguished Scholar Award**\n    *   **Award Amount:** $3,000\n    *   **Nomination Dates:** September 1 – April 1\n    *   **Eligibility:** Recognizes a researcher who has made outstanding contributions over a sustained period to the applied management accounting literature. Recognizes accomplishments of a mid-career or later nominee. Candidates must have received their terminal degree (e.g., Ph.D., DBA, Ed.D.) at least 10 years previously. This award may be awarded jointly to researchers who have collaborated extensively together.\n\n*   **Emerging Scholar Award**\n    *   **Award Amount:** $2,500\n    *   **Nomination Dates:** September 1 – April 1\n    *   **Eligibility:** Recognizes an early-career researcher who has made a meaningful and important contribution to the applied management accounting literature. Nominees must have published at least one single-authored manuscript or a co-authored article where they were the lead author. Nominees must have a terminal degree (e.g., Ph.D., DBA, Ed.D.) and have received their degree within the prior five years.\n</result>', extracted_content='<url>\nhttps://www.imanet.org/Membership/Academics/Research-Foundation\n</url>\n<query>\nExtract the \'IMA Research Grants\' section, including \'IMA Incubator Grant Program\', \'Academic Research Grant Program\', and \'Doctoral Scholars Program\'. For each program, extract the description, award amount, due date, eligibility, required documents, and application process. Also, extract information about the \'Distinguished Scholar Award\' and \'Emerging Scholar Award\', including award amount, nomination dates, and eligibility.\n</query>\n<result>\n**IMA Research Grants**\nTo submit a grant application for any of the grant programs, use the [IMA Application Portal](https://imaresearchgrants.secure-platform.com/a/organizations/main/home). Guidelines for Submitting Research Proposals are available [here](https://mc-69e30ef4-758e-4371-ac6f-2657-cdn-endpoint.azureedge.net/-/media/IMA/Files/Home/Membership/Academics/IMAResearchFoundationGuidelinesOct-2025-FINAL.ashx?rev=a88a5aad59ba429990dddb8865f02ec8&hash=75506F975C0BC10972D95A01C7B8CBDB).\n\n*   **IMA Incubator Grant Program**\n    *   **Description:** This program awards up to $5,000 for small Proof of Concept projects that will lead to more in-depth research.\n    *   **Award Amount:** Up to $5,000\n    *   **Due Date:** January 31.\n    *   **Eligibility:** Not explicitly stated in the provided content.\n    *   **Required Documents:** Not explicitly stated in the provided content.\n    *   **Applicatio