emory='Closed tab #CB47', extracted_content='Closed tab #CB47', include_extracted_content_only_once=False, metadata=None, include_in_memory=False), ActionResult(is_done=False, success=None, judgement=None, error=None, attachments=None, images=None, long_term_memory='Switched to tab #84C9', extracted_content='Switched to tab #84C9', include_extracted_content_only_once=False, metadata=None, include_in_memory=False), ActionResult(is_done=False, success=None, judgement=None, error=None, attachments=None, images=None, long_term_memory='Opened new tab with URL https://www.state.gov/bureaus-offices/under-secretary-for-civilian-security-democracy-and-human-rights/bureau-of-global-health-security-and-diplomacy/advancing-global-health-annual-program-statement-aps/', extracted_content='🔗  Opened new tab with url https://www.state.gov/bureaus-offices/under-secretary-for-civilian-security-democracy-and-human-rights/bureau-of-global-health-security-and-diplomacy/advancing-global-health-annual-program-statement-aps/', include_extracted_content_only_once=False, metadata=None, include_in_memory=False), ActionResult(is_done=False, success=None, judgement=None, error=None, attachments=None, images=None, long_term_memory='Closed tab #1E3A', extracted_content='Closed tab #1E3A', include_extracted_content_only_once=False, metadata=None, include_in_memory=False), ActionResult(is_done=False, success=None, judgement=None, error=None, attachments=None, images=None, long_term_memory='Switched to tab #84C9', extracted_content='Switched to tab #84C9', include_extracted_content_only_once=False, metadata=None, include_in_memory=False), ActionResult(is_done=False, success=None, judgement=None, error=None, attachments=None, images=None, long_term_memory=None, extracted_content='Clicked a "Establishing infrastructure hu..."', include_extracted_content_only_once=False, metadata=None, include_in_memory=False), ActionResult(is_done=False, success=None, judgement=None, error=None, attachments=None, images=None, long_term_memory='<url>\nhttps://wellcome.org/research-funding/schemes/establishing-infrastructure-hubs-power-evidence-synthesis#call-at-a-glance-ddd2\n</url>\n<query>\nExtract all information about the funding opportunity including funding amount, duration, eligibility criteria (who can apply, who can\'t apply), required documents, application process, key dates, and contact information.\n</query>\n<result>\n**Funding Opportunity: Establishing infrastructure hubs to power evidence synthesis in low- and middle-income countries**\n\n**Funding Amount:**\n*   £1.5 to £1.9 million\n*   Wellcome expects to make 5 awards.\n\n**Duration:**\n*   3-5 years\n\n**Eligibility Criteria:**\n\n**Who can apply:**\n*   **Lead applicant career stage:** Established researcher.\n*   **Administering organisation location:** Low- or middle-income countries (apart from mainland China).\n*   **Team:**\n    *   Teams of researchers (existing or new) with demonstrated expertise in evidence synthesis production, use, and dissemination.\n    *   From eligible organisations, based anywhere in the world (except mainland China), with the lead applicant based in a low- and middle-income country (LMIC).\n    *   Encouraged to bring diverse expertise, interdisciplinary collaborations, and researchers at various career stages.\n    *   Must include necessary expertise: evidence producers, methodologists, intermediaries, technologists, decision makers.\n    *   Must include a lead applicant or coapplicants based in each country where research will take place.\n    *   At least one applicant with significant demonstrated health expertise.\n    *   At least one applicant with significant demonstrated expertise in one of these policy sectors: food systems, humanitarian assistance, economic growth, peace and effective institutions, social protection.\n    *   Team size: at least four applicants (including lead), not exceeding eight applicants.\n    *   Must actively foster a diverse, inclusive, and supportive research environment and align with ESIC ‘Equity Companion’ document principles.\n*   **Lead applicant:**\n    *   Based at an organisation in an LMIC.\n    *   Demonstrated expertise in evidence synthesis production, use, and dissemination in their chosen sector.\n    *   Experience to lead collaborative, large-scale research projects with necessary support structures.\n    *   Permanent, open-ended, or long-term rolling contract (or guarantee of one) for the award duration, not conditional on receiving the award. If less than three years remaining, must have secured next position and provide a letter of support.\n    *   Based at an eligible organisation that can sign up to Wellcome\'s grant conditions.\n*   **Coapplicants:**\n    *   Can be based at the same or different organisations, including different countries, anywhere in the world (except mainland China).\n    *   Any career stage, from any relevant discipline. Up to seven coapplicants per team.\n    *   Must be essential for project delivery and make a significant contribution.\n    *   Must have a guarantee of space from their administering organisation for the duration of their commitment.\n    *   Must be based at an eligible organisation that can sign up to Wellcome\'s grant conditions (can include sole trader or self-employed person’s business).\n*   **Collaborators:** Support project delivery but do not lead. Do not need to meet eligibility requirements and are not counted in applicant numbers. Cannot receive salary, but expenses can be covered.\n*   **Time away from research:** Considered during application review.\n*   **Retirement:** Must contact Wellcome before applying; guarantee of space from administering organisation required.\n*   **Working part-time:** Lead and coapplicants can be part-time if compatible with project delivery.\n*   **Administering Organisation:**\n    *   Must be based in an LMIC (not mainland China).\n    *   Can be a higher education institution, research institute, healthcare organisation, or not-for-profit/non-governmental research organisation.\n    *   Multilateral organisations may be eligible (contact Wellcome for confirmation).\n    *   Must guarantee space and resources for applicants.\n    *   Must be able to sign up to Wellcome’s grant conditions.\n    *   Required to own all foreground intellectual property arising from the project and lead commercialisation activity.\n*   **Research Proposal Content:** Must include:\n    *   Creating a new global evidence infrastructure hub OR building on an existing one.\n    *   Focus on one of five sectors: food systems, humanitarian assistance, economic growth, peace and effective institutions, social protection.\n    *   Clear connection to at least one of Wellcome’s strategic priorities: Climate and Health, Infectious Disease, Mental Health, or Discovery Research.\n    *   Clear demonstration of how the infrastructure will be applied to at least one health challenge.\n    *   Connection to development/maintenance of sector-specific living evidence synthesis infrastructure (e.g., taxonomy, living evidence maps, AI-enabled LES, dynamic user-focused question banks, data repository, protocol registry).\n    *   Contributions to developing cross-sectoral standards for policy-scale AI-enabled LES.\n    *   Diverse interest holders contributing to co-production, testing, and piloting.\n    *   Plan to actively employ the ESIC collective impact approach.\n    *   Adherence to and promotion of open science principles (open source, open data standards).\n    *   Plan to develop and apply AI in line with RAISE guidance.\n\n**Who can\'t apply:**\n*   Applicants intending to carry out activities involving the transfer of funds into mainland China.\n*   Applicants who cannot demonstrate sufficient time and resources for the project.\n*   Applicants already on two applications for this call (can only be a lead applicant on one and a coapplicant on another, or a coapplicant on two, provided sufficient capacity and no overlap).\n*   Applicants who have already applied for, or hold, the maximum number of Wellcome awards.\n*   Members of the ESIC Steering Group.\n*   Commercial organisations as administering organisations.\n*   Research proposals that include the development of:\n    *   Evidence synthesis infrastructure not relevant or applicable to health and/or Wellcome’s strategic priorities.\n    *   Multiple infrastructure hubs.\n    *   An evidence synthesis infrastructure hub in a sector already addressed by previous ESIC investments (e.g., climate solutions, education, crime and justice, environment and sustainable development).\n\n**Required Documents:**\n*   Completed application form on the Wellcome Funding platform.\n*   A statement (up to 250 words) on how the proposed work aligns with current and future ESIC investments and the ESIC Roadmap, and how a collective impact approach will be employed (uploaded in the \'additional information\' section).\n*   Letter of support from the next eligible organisation if the lead applicant has less than three years remaining on their contract.\n*   Letter from the employing organisation confirming teaching commitment (if requesting teaching buyout).\n*   Letter from the Finance Director stating how overhead costs have been calculated (if applying for overheads).\n\n**Application Process:**\n1.  **Before you apply:** Read all information, watch the funding information webinar (recorded 18 March 2026), and view the sample application form. No need to contact Wellcome beforehand unless for specific support (e.g., disability, translation, multilateral organisation eligibility).\n2.  **Submit to administering organisation for approval:** Complete the application form on the Wellcome Funding Platform and submit it to your administering organisation\'s approver. Allow sufficient time for review and potential changes.\n3.  **Administering organisation approves and submits to Wellcome:** The application must be submitted by 15:00 BST on the deadline day. Late applications are not accepted. Wellcome will check eligibility and scope; ineligible applications will be withdrawn. Wellcome staff will review applications against assessment criteria. Shortlisted applications proceed.\n4.  **Committee review:** A committee, chosen for expertise and diversity, will review proposals and make funding recommendations.\n5.  **Funding decision:** Final decisions made by Wellcome. Applicants will receive an email notification in July 2026.\n*   **Support:** Disability-related support and certain translation costs are available. First-time applicant organisations must request an organisation account at least one week before the deadline.\n\n**Key Dates:**\n*   **18 March 2026:** Webinar (closed to new applications)\n*   **7 April 2026:** Scope check deadline (for sending a brief summary of your idea)\n*   **7 May 2026:** Application deadline (15:00 BST)\n*   **June 2026:** Committee review\n*   **July 2026:** Decision\n\n**Contact Information:**\n*   **Eligibility, what Wellcome offers, and application questions:** Use the "Send us a message" link on the website ([/about-us/contact-us/funding-enquiry](https://wellcome.org/about-us/contact-us/funding-enquiry)).\n*   **Scope questions:** Email [ESICSectoralHubs@wellcome.org](mailto:ESICSectoralHubs@wellcome.org) with a brief summary (no more than 200 words) by 7 April 2026. Include the call title in the subject line.\n*   **Other specific inquiries (e.g., multilateral organisation eligibility, housing cost calculation, sustainability initiatives approval, special needs education, translation costs):** Use the general "Contact us" link ([/about-us/contact-us/funding-enquiry](https://wellcome.org/about-us/contact-us/funding-enquiry)).\n</result>', extracted_content='<url>\nhttps://wellcome.org/research-funding/schemes/establishing-infrastructure-hubs-power-evidence-synthesis#call-at-a-glance-ddd2\n</url>\n<query>\nExtract all informati