e_extracted_content_only_once=False, metadata=None, include_in_memory=False), ActionResult(is_done=False, success=None, judgement=None, error=None, attachments=None, images=None, long_term_memory=None, extracted_content='Clicked a "PRIMA Section 1 - Thematic Are..."', include_extracted_content_only_once=False, metadata=None, include_in_memory=False), ActionResult(is_done=False, success=None, judgement=None, error=None, attachments=None, images=None, long_term_memory='<url>\nhttps://prima-med.org/submit-your-project/water-management-in-the-nexus/\n</url>\n<query>\nExtract all information about the funding opportunity including funding amount, duration, eligibility criteria (who can apply, who can\'t apply), required documents, application process, key dates, and contact information.\n</query>\n<result>\n**Funding Opportunity Title:** Call: Thematic Area 1-Water Management in the Nexus (TOPIC: 1.1.1-2026 (IA): Decentralised Brackish Water Desalination for Climate-Resilient and Resource-Efficient Mediterranean Agriculture)\n\n**Funding Amount:**\nEUR 10.815 million (Total indicative amount allocated to this call)\n\n**Duration:**\nThe webpage does not specify the duration of the projects.\n\n**Eligibility Criteria:**\n*   Solutions should be co-designed with relevant stakeholders including farmers, water user associations, community organisations, and public authorities.\n*   Proposals must adopt a Multi-Actor Approach (MAA), ensuring meaningful involvement of all key actors: end users, practitioners, SMEs, technology providers, researchers, and competent authorities throughout the project lifecycle.\n*   Projects should include strong contributions from agronomy, water and resource management, socio-economics, and relevant Social Sciences and Humanities (SSH).\n*   Meaningful involvement of SMEs is expected.\n*   Consortia are encouraged to apply the Societal Readiness Thinking Tool.\n\n**Required Documents:**\n*   Annual Work Programme 2026\n*   Guidelines for Applicants Section 1\n*   KPI Handbook\n*   Electronic Submission System Handbook\n*   Full Proposal Template RIA&IA PART-I\n*   Full Proposal Template RIA&IA PART-II\n*   Call text Topic 1.1.1-2026 Water management in the Nexus\n\n**Application Process:**\n*   Submission is via an electronic system, with a link provided: [https://aap.agencerecherche.fr/_layouts/15/SIM/Pages/SIMNouveauProjet.aspx?idAAP=2395](https://aap.agencerecherche.fr/_layouts/15/SIM/Pages/SIMNouveauProjet.aspx?idAAP=2395)\n*   The process involves a "Stage 2" submission.\n\n**Key Dates:**\n*   Opening Date: 20.03.2026\n*   Submission Deadline Stage 2: 29.09.2026 (17:00h Central European Time (CET))\n*   Status: Closed\n\n**Contact Information:**\n*   Prof. Ali Rhouma: [ali.rhouma@prima-med.org](mailto:ali.rhouma@prima-med.org)\n*   Main Office:\n    Nexus 2 Building,\n    Carrer Jordi Girona 29, 2nd floor 2A\n    08034 Barcelona\n    Phone: +34 930 19 08 23\n</result>', extracted_content='<url>\nhttps://prima-med.org/submit-your-project/water-management-in-the-nexus/\n</url>\n<query>\nExtract all information about the funding opportunity including funding amount, duration, eligibility criteria (who can apply, who can\'t apply), required documents, application process, key dates, and contact information.\n</query>\n<result>\n**Funding Opportunity Title:** Call: Thematic Area 1-Water Management in the Nexus (TOPIC: 1.1.1-2026 (IA): Decentralised Brackish Water Desalination for Climate-Resilient and Resource-Efficient Mediterranean Agriculture)\n\n**Funding Amount:**\nEUR 10.815 million (Total indicative amount allocated to this call)\n\n**Duration:**\nThe webpage does not specify the duration of the projects.\n\n**Eligibility Criteria:**\n*   Solutions should be co-designed with relevant stakeholders including farmers, water user associations, community organisations, and public authorities.\n*   Proposals must adopt a Multi-Actor Approach (MAA), ensuring meaningful involvement of all key actors: end users, practitioners, SMEs, technology providers, researchers, and competent authorities throughout the project lifecycle.\n*   Projects should include strong contributions from agronomy, water and resource management, socio-economics, and relevant Social Sciences and Humanities (SSH).\n*   Meaningful involvement of SMEs is expected.\n*   Consortia are encouraged to apply the Societal Readiness Thinking Tool.\n\n**Required Documents:**\n*   Annual Work Programme 2026\n*   Guidelines for Applicants Section 1\n*   KPI Handbook\n*   Electronic Submission System Handbook\n*   Full Proposal Template RIA&IA PART-I\n*   Full Proposal Template RIA&IA PART-II\n*   Call text Topic 1.1.1-2026 Water management in the Nexus\n\n**Application Process:**\n*   Submission is via an electronic system, with a link provided: [https://aap.agencerecherche.fr/_layouts/15/SIM/Pages/SIMNouveauProjet.aspx?idAAP=2395](https://aap.agencerecherche.fr/_layouts/15/SIM/Pages/SIMNouveauProjet.aspx?idAAP=2395)\n*   The process involves a "Stage 2" submission.\n\n**Key Dates:**\n*   Opening Date: 20.03.2026\n*   Submission Deadline Stage 2: 29.09.2026 (17:00h Central European Time (CET))\n*   Status: Closed\n\n**Contact Information:**\n*   Prof. Ali Rhouma: [ali.rhouma@prima-med.org](mailto:ali.rhouma@prima-med.org)\n*   Main Office:\n    Nexus 2 Building,\n    Carrer Jordi Girona 29, 2nd floor 2A\n    08034 Barcelona\n    Phone: +34 930 19 08 23\n</result>', include_extracted_content_only_once=False, metadata=None, include_in_memory=False), ActionResult(is_done=False, success=None, judgement=None, error=None, attachments=None, images=None, long_term_memory='Successfully replaced all occurrences of "- [x] Collect Funding Information (Funding Programs: Research Grant Programme, Targeted Grants in Mathematics and Physical Sciences (MPS), Global Innovation Fund Program, Innovating for Climate Resilience Fund, Small Grants for African Heritage Projects, Fund for Innovation in Development Grant Program, Hum